desc:Empress [Arcana synth] (GFX)
//tags: instrument synth polyphonic pad lead deep house sidechain pump chorus phaser autopan delay reverb arcana
//author: GardenFX
// by JGWizrad / Garden FX (GFX)
//
// Requires gfx-drift, gfx-output, gfx-ui, gfx-panel, gfx-instrument and gfx-s57 (.jsfx-inc) in the same folder.
//
// THE EMPRESS (card III of the GFX Arcana series): fertility, abundance, sensual warmth, the earth that grounds it all.
// A breathing deep-house pad machine. One keyboard plays three layers at once; each layer has its own compressor,
// keyed by an internal "fake kick" that keeps the host's time, so the pads pump and swell with the groove - from
// hypnotic 90s deep-house warmth to huge, slowly breathing ambient pads.
//   OSC 1, OSC 2   two Juno-style pad layers (8 voices): one oscillator with SAW, PULSE (PW, and PWM from the layer's
//              own LFO: PWM depth, RATE), SUB (a square an octave down), NOISE; DETUNE (cents); a 24 dB ladder low-pass
//              (CUTOFF, RESO, ENV - the amp envelope opens it, KEY tracking fixed); an ATT / DEC / SUS / REL envelope.
//   OSC 3      a Moog / Prophet-style lead layer: two oscillators (A and B, SAW or PULSE each - lit keys), B's COARSE
//              and FINE tuning, MIX, PW; a ladder (CUTOFF, RESO, ENV, F.DEC - the filter envelope's decay);
//              ATT / DEC / SUS / REL; GLIDE, VIBRATO (the mod wheel adds more); POLY / MONO / LEGATO for this layer.
//   Every layer: ON (lit key, faded), LEVEL (the fader), PAN, OCTAVE, and KEY 0 - 10: how deep the kick ducks it
//              (0 = not at all, 10 = a deep, classic house pump - about 24 dB).
//   THE PULSE  the fake kick (Deep16's kick, synthesised): it follows REAPER's tempo and beat position when the
//              transport runs, and keeps time from the tempo on its own when it is stopped (so the pads breathe while
//              you audition). RUN (on by default, so the pads pump from insert); the division: 1/4, 1/8, 1/2, or
//              1/4+ (on the beats, plus a lighter off-beat pump between them - the off-beats duck at 60 % and make no
//              kick sound). KICK: its level (silent at 0, the default: it only keys the ducking); TONE (its pitch and
//              drop), DECAY. The kick goes to the output after the effects, never through them.
//              DUCK RELEASE: how fast the layers swell back after each hit. SHAPE: the swell's curve, from a quick
//              recovery (left), through linear, to the classic held-down-then-bloom pump (right). Every duck is an
//              envelope-shaped gain (a 3 ms raised-cosine attack, then the release curve), never a gate.
//   THE FX CHAIN (each with its lit keys): BBD CHORUS (I, II - both lit: I+II), DYNATRON PHASER (a 6-stage phaser:
//              RATE, DEPTH, COLOUR - the feedback), the MULTI-BAND AUTOPAN (three bands split by Linkwitz-Riley
//              crossovers, LOW X and HIGH X, so the bands sum flat: each band its own RATE and DEPTH fader - the lows
//              narrow and slow by default so the bass stays centred - and GLOBAL, a rate multiplier for all three),
//              then the DELAY (synced: TIME; FDBK, TONE, MIX) and the REVERB (SIZE, DECAY, DAMP, MIX) as sends, each
//              with its own KEY 0 - 10 ducking its wet tail under the kick. The two sends' MIX follow the send law:
//              the dry signal stays at full level up to 50 %, the wet rises to full by 50 %.
//   FATE       the series' drift (0 - 100 %, 50 % = the standard amount) - here breathing growth: the pads' detune,
//              their pulse widths and their filters wander slowly, and the three autopan bands' rates drift apart
//              and back together.
//   VOLUME, LEVEL, VELOCITY (how much the touch matters), SAT (the output soft clip is always on).
//   TERRACOTTA / MOSS: the faceplate's finish.
// The display: the autopan's three bands (the spectrum, upright, with its two crossovers; each band's place in the
// stereo field as a moving marker) and the ducking over the last bar (the kick's hits and each layer's gain
// reduction, live).
// MIDI: notes, pitch bend (+/- 2), CC1 (more vibrato on OSC 3), CC64 sustain, CC120 / CC123 all notes off.

import gfx-drift.jsfx-inc
import gfx-output.jsfx-inc
import gfx-ui.jsfx-inc
import gfx-panel.jsfx-inc
import gfx-instrument.jsfx-inc
import gfx-s57.jsfx-inc

